{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-language golden vectors for the domain strength receipt.",
    "",
    "WHY: the strength summary is computed by the Python engine (under Pyodide) but",
    "SIGNED in TypeScript by @gainratio/avow. That split is only sound if both sides",
    "canonicalize a subject to the SAME bytes. These vectors are the proof, not an",
    "assertion: they were produced by the Python `avow` kernel (RFC 8785 via rfc8785",
    "+ Ed25519 via PyNaCl) over a REAL DomainStrengthSubject shape.",
    "",
    "Both suites consume this one file:",
    "  backend/tests/test_strength_receipt_vectors.py  re-derives them with Python avow",
    "  frontend/packages/browser/src/pyodide/__tests__/strengthReceipt.test.ts  with TS avow",
    "",
    "The subjects deliberately stress JCS number formatting, where a naive JSON",
    "encoder diverges: 60.0 -> 60, 5.0 -> 5, 1e-07 -> 1e-7, and a 12-significant-digit",
    "float that needs shortest-round-trip encoding.",
    "",
    "The seed is 0x02*32, deliberately distinct from the assay repo's own envelope",
    "vectors (0x01*32) so the two conformance suites can never alias.",
    "",
    "Re-mint after an avow envelope change (avow 0.5 added the required",
    "receipt `schema`): cd backend && uv run python tools/mint_strength_receipt_vectors.py"
  ],
